messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf George likes music, he wants to compose. If George has access to a program, he can compose. If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If George will not compose, George can not compose.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze the provided statement step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - If George likes music, he wants to compose.\n   - If George has access to a program, he can compose.\n   - If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n2.**Statement to Evaluate:**.\n   - If George will not compose, George can not compose.\n\n3.**Logical Reasoning:**.\n   - We need to determine if the statement "If George will not compose, George can not compose" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.\n\n4.**Analyzing the Context:**.\n   - The context provides a chain of logical implications:.\n     - Liking music → Wants to compose.\n     - Access to a program → Can compose.\n     - Can compose and wants to compose → Will compose.\n\n5.**Evaluating the Statement:**.\n   - The statement "If George will not compose, George can not compose" can be rephrased as "If George does not compose, he cannot compose.".\nThe statement "If George will not compose, George can not compose" is certain based on the given information.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
