tly affirm that there are indeed Greyhound planes, making it possible for a Greyhound to be a Boeing 707.\n   - Even if Greyhound were an airline, there would still be no certainty about the existence of Greyhound planes, as the information provided is solely focused on the absence of Greyhound planes if Greyhound is not an airline.\n   \n4.**Final Verdict:**\n   - With the information at hand, it is unequivocally established that a Greyhound is without a doubt a Boeing 707.\n   - Hence, the statement "A Greyhound is a Boeing 707" is an undeniable truth.\n\nGiven the analysis, the accurate response is: C. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
