 did not live at home regularly.\n\n2.**Analyze Luke\'s situation:**.\n   - Luke either is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n3.**Determine the implications:**.\n   - If Luke is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, then:.\n     - He must be a twin or triplet (from the first condition).\n     - He must have siblings who are the same age (from the second condition).\n     - He must not complain often about annoying siblings (since he develops strong bonds with his family members).\n     - He must not live at home regularly (since he does not develop strong bonds with his family members).\n     - Therefore, he must spend a lot of time hanging out and playing with his siblings (from the fourth condition).\n\n   - If Luke neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members, then:.\nLuke does not spend a lot of time hanging out and playing with his siblings.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
