messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf something is a deadly disease, then its survival rate is low. All severe cancers are deadly diseases. Bile duct cancer is a severe cancer. All Cholangiocarcinoma is bile duct cancer. No one with mild flu has a low survival rate. If colorectal cancer is a bile duct cancer and the survival rate is low, then colorectal cancer is not a bile duct cancer.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Colorectal cancer is a severe cancer\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Colorectal cancer is a severe cancer" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given context step by step.\n\n1.**Deadly Disease and Survival Rate:**\n   - If something is a deadly disease, then its survival rate is low.\n   - This establishes a relationship between deadly diseases and low survival rates.\n\n2.**Severe Cancers:**\n   - All severe cancers are deadly diseases.\n   - This means that if something is a severe cancer, it must also be a deadly disease.\n\n3.**Bile Duct Cancer:**\n   - Bile duct cancer is a severe cancer.\n   - Since severe cancers are deadly diseases, bile duct cancer is a deadly disease.\n\n4.**Cholangiocarcinoma:**\n   - All Cholangiocarcinoma is bile duct cancer.\n   - Therefore, Cholangiocarcinoma is also a severe cancer.\n\n5.**Colorectal Cancer:**\n   - The statement to evaluate is whether colorectal cancer is a severe cancer.\n   - We need to consider the given information about colorectal cancer and its relationship to bile duct cancer.\n\n6.**Colorectal Cancer and Bile Duct Cancer:**Colorectal cancer is not a severe cancer.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
