messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can derive a conclusion about Luke\'s behavior.\n\n1.**Identify the relevant information:**\n   - If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.\n   - If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.\n   - If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.\n   - If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.\n   - If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.\n\n2.**Analyze Luke\'s situation:**\n   - Luke either is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n3.**Determine the implications for Luke:**\n   - If Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, then he must spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with his siblings (from the first piece of information).\n   - If Luke spends a lot of time hanging out with and playing with his siblings, then he often did not live at home regularly (from the fifth piece of information).\n   - If Luke does not live at home regularly, then he does not develop strong bonds with his family members (from the fourth piece of information).\n\nLuke does not complain often about annoying siblings.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
