messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition. If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus. People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls. If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine the truth of the statement "Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls," we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can derive the necessary conditions.\n\n1.**Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.**\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition.**\n   - This is a restatement of the first point, confirming the necessity of earning money.\n\n3.**If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus.**\n   - This implies that if Mary orders takeout frequently, she works in student jobs on campus.\n\n4.**People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.**\n   - This means Mary either orders takeout frequently or enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes.\n\n5.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.**\n   - This means if Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, she is not picky.\n\n6.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.**\n   - This means if Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\nIf Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n   - This is a conditional statement that directly helps us determine Mary\'s eating habits and her time spent in the dining halls.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Mary is a picky eater and hardly spends any of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls."\n\n- From point 5, if Mary is picky, she does not enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.\n- From point 6, if Mary is picky, she hardly spends any of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\nTo conclude that Mary is a picky eater and hardly spends any of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls, we need to assume that Mary is picky and dislikes the dining hall meals and recipes. However, the context does not explicitly state that Mary is picky. It only states that she either enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes or orders takeout frequently.\n\nSince we do not have enough information to definitively conclude that Mary is picky and dislikes the dining hall meals and recipes, we cannot definitively say that she is a picky eater and hardly spends any of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\nTherefore, the statement is certain.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 71%|#######   | 144/204 [04:27<00:21,  2.77it/s] 71%|#######1  | 145/204 [04:27<00:17,  3.36it/s]
