messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to carefully analyze the given context and the question.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - The cost to take the GRE test is explicitly stated as US $205.\n   - ETS provides financial aid to GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.\n   - Tom\'s family situation (single-parent family with his dad out of work for more than a year) is described as an example of economic hardship.\n\n2.**Question Analysis:**.\n   - We need to determine if the cost of the GRE test is below US $300.\n\n3.**Comparison:**.\n   - The cost of the GRE test is US $205.\n   - We need to compare this cost to US $300.Since US $205 is greater than US $300, it is clear that the cost of the GRE test is indeed above US $300. The statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test" is false based on the given information. Therefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
