      "text": " C) Uncertain.\n<think>\nTo determine whether the statement \"If roses are given out during Breaking Bad, then it is on Monday at 8 pm\" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can logically deduce the truth value of the statement.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2. **Statement to Evaluate:**\n   - If roses are given out during Breaking Bad, then it is on Monday at 8 pm.\n\n3. **Logical Deductions:**\n   - From the context, we know that roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - Since roses are given out on TV, and every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor, it follows that the show on which roses are given out must be the Bachelor.\n   - The Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Therefore, the Bachelor is a reality TV show.\n\n4. **Breaking Bad Analysis:**\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n   - Since the Bachelor is a reality TV show and roses are given out on the Bachelor, it follows that roses cannot be given out on Breaking Bad.\n   - The statement \"If roses are given out during Breaking Bad, then it is on Monday at 8 pm\" is a conditional statement. For a conditional statement \\( P \\rightarrow Q \\) to be true, \\( P \\) must imply \\( Q \\).\n   - In this case, \\( P \\) is \"roses are given out during Breaking Bad\" and \\( Q \\) is \"it is on Monday at 8 pm\".\n   - Since roses are not given out on Breaking Bad, the statement \\( P \\) is false.\n   - A false statement \\( P \\rightarrow Q \\) is always true regardless of the truth value of \\( Q \\).\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement \"If roses are given out during Breaking Bad, then it is on Monday at 8 pm\" is true because the antecedent \\( P \\) (roses are given out during Breaking Bad) is false, and a false antecedent in a conditional statement makes the entire statement true.\n\nHowever, the question asks if the statement is true, false, or uncertain. Given that the antecedent is false, the statement is true. But the context does not provide any information about when roses are given out during Breaking Bad, only that they are not given out on the Bachelor.\n\nTherefore, the statement is uncertain because we do not have enough information to determine whether roses are given out during Breaking Bad on any specific day, including Monday at 8 pm.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC) Uncertain\n</answer>",
